From 2f531ab64465bf1b52e6aefb1feb815b21000d4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 08:58:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06868/11362] [outer-loop] ARC s5i5 round-4: L4->L7,
 three-level jump in one session

Round-4 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on s5i5 directly cracks round-3's "E/9
and C/9 couplings" deadlock and clears three levels in one session:

- L5: temporarily grow E through the upper F-wall gap to lift the 9 rail;
  once the attached 1-column retracts above the isolated F block, 9 can
  retract past C, E retracts, C lowers the diamond carrier below both F
  walls, and E regrows into the lower socket.
- L6: a three-link telescoping arm with active 90-degree joint rotators;
  folding E-left/B-down/9-right routes it through the wall corridor.
- L7: a four-link articulated maze plus a separate A/8 clearance coupling
  (B-down, E-left, a temporarily-horizontal 9 segment, 9-up, C-right).

Fresh-reset reproduce() self-verified L5+L6 (202-action prefix,
reached_level=6). L7 was won live at step 431; the source agent's overall
reproduction_verified is correctly false (gating the full 311-action line
would have exceeded budget), but the outer loop independently verified it:
5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new resolver priority branch, all 5
confirmed level=7, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

L8 was scouted (movable carriage + diamond carrier + rotated chamber
cross) but not solved -- budget ran out after decoding the controls.

reproducible_total_levels 149 -> 152. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
